  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 157 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nUpper ridging starts to nudge into the Western Plains tonight,\narriving fully over the CWA by Saturday. Surface high pressure\ntonight will bring light winds and good radiational cooling, but\nthink there will be more cloud cover than the model blends show.\nHave temps bottoming out in the teens still as there should be a\nsharp drop after sunset before clouds fill back in. Temps\ntomorrow will be similar today and near seasonal averages. Upper\nridging will continue through the weekend and into early next\nweek, with pretty good agreement from the ensemble members on\ntemps warming back up above normal. Highs look to be back up\ninto the 50s by Monday.\n\nStill some variation in the details with how the upper ridge\nbreaks down and split flow trough comes into the Plains. Some of\nthe clusters track the low along the Canadian border, while\nother solutions start the system out over the Central Plains.\nProbabilities of measurable precipitation are decent, around 40\npercent, so at least some areas will get some moisture. With the\nECMWF EFI still showing a signal for warmth, most likely form\nof precipitation will be rain.",
